<title>USA: USDA grain advisory panel to meet April 16-17.</title>
<headline>USDA grain advisory panel to meet April 16-17.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Thursday said the Grain Inspection, Packers and Stockyards Administration's (GIPSA) grain inspection advisory committee will meet here on April 16 and 17.</p>
<p>USDA said topics on the agenda will include hedge-to-arrive contracts, grain inspection automation policy and a briefing on the ConAgra Inc investigation and plea agreement.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, ConAgra agreed to pay $8.3 million to settle federal charges made against its Peavey Co unit over grain handling.</p>
</text>
